;; clojure-lsp configuration for glitter.
;;
;; glitter is a library — its whole point is a public API other projects
;; call, not one this repo calls internally end-to-end. Without this,
;; `clojure-lsp diagnostics` flags every genuinely-public entry point
;; (glitter.app/run, glitter.alias/defalias, glitter.env/dev?, ...) as
;; "unused", which is simply wrong for a library and would make the
;; linter noisy rather than a useful signal.
;;
;; :source-paths is pinned explicitly to src+test. clojure-lsp's default
;; source-path discovery only auto-includes extra-paths declared on
;; aliases literally named :dev or :test (its built-in :source-aliases
;; default) — every other alias here (:crud, :flights, :counter, ...)
;; declares :extra-paths ["examples"] for `jolt -M:<alias>` purposes only
;; and was never visible to clojure-lsp's own project analysis. Found
;; live while wiring :temperature's test coverage: deps.edn's :test
;; alias needed "examples" added to its OWN :extra-paths so `jolt -M:test`
;; can require glitter.temperature from temperature_test.clj — but doing
;; that made clojure-lsp's default discovery suddenly treat "examples" as
;; a real source-path too (since it's now reachable via the recognized
;; :test alias), surfacing ~27 pre-existing, unrelated formatting
;; deviations across examples/*.clj that predate this change and are out
;; of scope for it. Pinning :source-paths here decouples clojure-lsp's
;; view from deps.edn's per-alias :extra-paths entirely, preserving the
;; status quo (examples/ has never actually been covered by
;; `bb lsp:format-check`/`bb lsp:diagnostics`, despite the
;; README's "whole codebase is bb lsp:format-check-clean" claim — that
;; claim is about src+test, not examples; a real gap, but a separate
;; follow-up, not this task's to fix). `bb lint`/`clj-kondo` are
;; unaffected — they take explicit "src test examples" directory args on
;; the command line, not clojure-lsp's alias-based discovery.
{:linters {:clojure-lsp/unused-public-var {:level :off}}
 :source-paths #{"src" "test"}}
